t overwritten when the logo was drawn? No.\n\nHmm, actually maybe the pause happened on a frame where the HUD re-draw... Actually reset then screenshot then pause. Between screenshot and pause, frames advanced. Title screen animation may wipe TIME? Unlikely.\n\nLet me just re-read the nametable row 3 alone and also check get_tile_at_pixel at TIME digit location, e.g. screen (205,25) roughly. TIME label at cols 25-28 => x 200-231. Digits 397 at cols 25-27, row 3 => y 24-31, x 200-223.\n\nScreen: TIME label appears around x 200-232. In the screenshot \"TIME\" at x~200-230, \"397\" below at x~205-228. Let me get_tile_at_pixel at (210,27).\n\nAlso let me read_nametable for the logo tile range. The logo object region returned a truncated bounding box but tiles list. It said box (40,38)-(91,101) truncated, continuing beyond window. The full logo probably spans a region. Let me get_region again at a bigger representative point maybe center of logo, but object mode always uses 64x64 window and truncates. Better to read the nametable over the logo area to get tile range. The logo is roughly rows 5-14, cols 4-27. Let me read_nametable 0,4 28x12.\n\nActually the task says: \"The title logo ... get_region in object mode on it (the proof), and record it with record_mapping mapping_type note, id 'title logo', naming its tile range and pattern table.\"\n\nSo I should name its tile range (e.g. CHR $1C0-$1FF? or tile ids) and pattern table ($1000). Let me read the nametable over the logo to determine which tile ids it uses.\n\nLet me do: read_nametable 0 0,4 width 32 height 16 (rows 4-19) to capture the logo tiles. And get_tile_at_pixel at (210,27).\n\nAlso note: the title logo's tiles — let me look at what chr_tiles. The get_region listed tiles [294,322,323,324,326,328,464,465,...]. But that's only within the 64x64 window at (28,38). Hmm.\n\nBetter approach: read_nametable over logo to get tile ids, then convert: tile_id + 0x100 = chr_tile. The region listed \"background CHR 0x126,