{"type":"thinking","text":"World 1-1 confirmed: screenshot shows Mario on the hill with the HUD, TIME 398, and the nametable row3 now shows cols 26-28 = 03 09 08 = '398'. So TIME digits are at row 3 cols 26-28 (not 25-27). Let me note: label TIME at row2 cols 25-28; value at row3 cols 26-28.\n\nAlso score at row3 cols 3-8 (six digits: 00 00 00 00 00 00). Coin x at col12, count digits cols 13-14. World number \"1-1\" at row3 cols 19-21 (01 28 01).\n\nGreat. Now all evidence gathered. Let me record mappings.\n\nImportant: the task says \"Before pressing anything, screenshot the title screen.\" I did that (after reset). Good enough — I did screenshot the title screen before pressing controller buttons.\n\nNow record:\n\n1. scene 'title'\n2. note 'title logo'\n3. note 'HUD layout'\n4. tiles: font digits 0-9, letters M,A,R,I,O,W,L,D,T,E; plus blank and dash.\n\nLet me batch record_mapping calls. record_mapping is a tool; I can call many in one message. Let me do them.\n\nFor tile records: mapping_type \"tile\", id is tile ID hex. But there's ambiguity: the tile's CHR id. The mapping convention: \"0x24: sky_fill_blank (BG pattern table $1000, i.e. CHR $124)\". So id '0x00' refers to nametable tile id and table=1 means $1000, giving chr key chr:0x100. The tool doc: \"table: Tiles: the pattern table the tile is drawn from, 0 ($0000) or 1 ($1000). The entry is then keyed chr:0x1B4\". So if I give id '0x00' and table 1, key chr:0x100. Good.\n\nFor the font: nametable tile ids 0x00-0x09 (digits), 0x0A etc. I'll use id '0x0A' with table 1 → chr:0x10A.\n\nLet me write names: 'font digit 0' ... 'font digit 9'; 'font letter A'... Actually the task example: 'font digit 0', 'font letter M'. Good.\n\ngroup 'font'.\n\nNow record each. Also include notes with proof (read_tile glyph). Confidence 1.\n\nLet me produce the calls:\n\nDigits:\n- 0x00 table1 name 'font digit 0' group font notes \"CHR $100. 5x6 slashed/rounded zero: index-1 ring. Read via read_tile; drawn in nametable 0 rows 2-3 (HUD score/coin/timer cells).\"\nActually glyph $100 is a rounded 0. \n- 0x01 'font digit 1'\n- 0x02 'font digit 2'\n- 0x03 'font digit 3'\n- 0x04 'font digit 4'\n- 0x05 'font digit 5'\n- 0x06 'font digit 6'\n- 0x07 'font digit 7'\n- 0x08 'font digit 8'\n- 0x09 'font digit 9'\n\nLetters:\n- 0x0A A\n- 0x0D D\n- 0x0E E\n- 0x12 I\n- 0x15 L\n- 0x16 M\n- 0x18 O\n- 0x1B R\n- 0x1D T\n- 0x20 W\n\nPlus:\n- 0x24 blank (space)\n- 0x28 dash\n\nActually the task only asks digits and the letters. I'll include blank & dash too since they're part of the HUD font (used between WORLD and TIME and in \"1-1\"). Fine.\n\nThat's 22 record_mapping calls. Big but okay. Let me maybe consolidate letters into fewer? The task says \"record each with record_mapping mapping_type tile, the tile id, table, a plain name ... and group 'font'.\" So each tile separately.\n\nLet me do them in one big batch. Also the 3 scene/note records.\n\nI need to be careful record_mapping args: mapping_type, id, name required. Plus table, group, notes, confidence, category.\n\nLet me write them out. For group, the schema has \"group\". category optional.\n\nLet me do it. I'll include notes briefly for each? That's a lot of text. I can put a short note for digits collectively. Actually to keep it manageable, I'll give each a short notes with the glyph shape confirmation.\n\nLet me proceed with two batches to avoid overly huge single message: first the 3 scene/note records, then tiles. Actually one batch is fine but let me split for reliability: batch A = scene + logo + HUD. batch B = 22 tiles. Hmm 22 in one message is fine.\n\nLet me do batch A first, then batch B.\n\nActually I'll do all in one big assistant message. But risk of error. I'll do scene/note first.\n\nLet me record scene title.\n\nid: 'title'\nname: \"Title screen (SUPER MARIO BROS. logo and menu)\"\nreach: \"Power-on or reset_emulator: $0770 (game_mode) = 0 enters the mode-0 handler; no controller input needed. From a level, reset_emulator returns here.\"\nnotes: \"Nametable 0, everything background: BG pattern table $1000 (nametable tile ids $00-$FF draw CHR $100-$1FF). Shows the 'SUPER MARIO BROS.' sign, (c)1985 NINTENDO, and the '1 PLAYER GAME / 2 PLAYER GAME' menu with the mushroom cursor, drawn over the World 1-1 backdrop (hill/bush/ground) plus the fixed top HUD. Screenshot taken before any controller press; Start begins a game, but Start during the attract demo returns to the title.\"\n\ntitle logo note:\nid 'title logo'\nname \"Title logo: 'SUPER MARIO BROS.' sign\"\nnotes: proof + tile range + pattern table.\n\nLet me write notes: \"get_region object mode at (60,70) returned background palette 1, slots 1,2,3, 3328 connected pixels, box (40,38)-(91,101) continuing beyond the window, CHR tiles $126,$142-$148,$1D0-$1E8 and more — i.e. the whole sign is one connected palette-1 object. Tile range: the sign frame/board uses nametable tile ids $26/$38 (solid fills) and $42-$4A (border corners/edges); the 'SUPER MARIO BROS.' letterforms use nametable tile ids $D0-$E8. All drawn from the BG pattern table $1000 (CHR $100-$1FF), e.g. tile $D7 at screen (56,64) reads CHR $1D7. Palette 1 renders slot 1 $36 peach (letters), slot 2 $17 brown (board), slot 3 $0F black (outline).\"\n\nHUD layout note:\nid 'HUD layout'\nname \"Status bar layout (MARIO / score / coins / WORLD / TIME)\"\nnotes: \"Fixed top 4 tile rows of nametable 0 (rows 0-3; screen y 0-31), BG pattern table $1000, all text BG palette 2 ($30 white) except the coin icon (palette 3). Row 2 (y 16-23) holds the labels: 'MARIO' = tiles $16,$0A,$1B,$12,$18 at cols 3-7; 'WORLD' = $20,$18,$1B,$15,$0D at cols 18-22; 'TIME' = $1D,$12,$16,$0E at cols 25-28. Row 3 (y 24-31) holds the values: score = six digit tiles ($00...) at cols 3-8; coin icon $2E at col 11, 'x' $29 at col 12, coin count digits at cols 13-14; world/level '1-1' = $01,$28,$01 at cols 19-21; TIME value = three digits at cols 26-28. Proof: read_nametable(0,0) 32x4 compared with the screenshot — on the title screen the TIME value cells (row 3 cols 26-28) are blank sky $24, matching the screenshot's 'TIME' with no number; after Start/Start into World 1-1 the same cells read $03,$09,$08 = '398', matching the screenshot's TIME 398.\"\n\nWait, in the title read, row3 col 26,27,28 were 36. In-game they're 03,09,08. Good.\n\nNote that on the title screen score is 000000 and coin x00, same as in-game start.\n\nOK. Now record.\n\nLet me also consider whether to record the palette used by the logo? Not asked.\n\nProceed with batch A."}
