{"type":"text","text":"Done — Mapping sheet 1 for Super Mario Bros. is recorded and promoted.\n\n**What I did**\n\n1. **Title screen** — Screenshot taken before pressing any controller button (after a soft reset to get back from the stray World 1-1 state). Recorded as scene `title` with reach and notes naming the pattern table (`$1000`, nametable ids `$00-$FF` → CHR `$100-$1FF`).\n2. **Title logo** — `get_region` in object mode at (60,70) returned one connected background object, palette 1, slots 1-3, 3328 px, CHR tiles `$126`, `$142-$148`, `$1D0-$1E8`. Recorded as note `title logo`: sign frame/board = nametable ids `$26`/`$38`/`$42-$4A`, letterforms = `$D0-$E8`, all from BG pattern table `$1000`, palette 1 ($36 peach letters, $17 brown board, $0F outline).\n3. **HUD layout** — `read_nametable` rows 0-3 compared against screenshots. Row 2 labels: MARIO cols 3-7, WORLD cols 18-22, TIME cols 25-28. Row 3 values: score cols 3-8, coin icon/x/count cols 11-14, \"1-1\" cols 19-21, TIME value cols 26-28. The proof is that the TIME cells are blank on the title screen but read `$03,$09,$08` = \"398\" in play, matching the in-game screenshot.\n4. **Font** — `read_tile` confirmed the glyphs at CHR `$100-$109` (digits 0-9), letters A/D/E/I/L/M/O/R/T/W at `$10A`/`$10D`/`$10E`/`$112`/`$115`/`$116`/`$118`/`$11B`/`$11D`/`$120`, plus blank `$124` and hyphen `$128`. Each recorded as a `tile` entry, table 1, group `font`.\n5. **Start/Start** — `play_input` Start (6f), wait 60f, Start (6f), wait 150f; screenshot confirmed World 1-1 began (Mario on the hill).\n6. **promote_mappings** — 25 confirmed discoveries promoted to the shared mapping file (now 53 tiles, 8 palettes, 2 sprites, 26 addresses). Game left running.\n\nOne correction worth noting: on the title screen the timer cells are empty (only the \"TIME\" label draws), so \"TIME 397/398\" is an in-game HUD state, not a title-screen one."}
